Package: tokenmonitor
Version: 2.4.3
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 150
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, wmctrl
Maintainer: Alessandro Gonçalves <10013256+aleinconnext@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/aleinconnext/tokenmonitor
Description: desktop usage monitor for Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and FreeLLMAPI
 A native GTK4 widget with one circular gauge per assistant, in the
 spirit of codenotch for macOS. The window is frameless and translucent,
 can be anchored to any screen edge or corner, and optionally stays
 always on top.
 .
 Gauges stack vertically when the window is docked to a side and sit
 side by side at the top or bottom. Drag the window with the mouse:
 releasing it near an edge snaps it into place (side anchors switch to
 the vertical layout automatically) and the position is remembered
 between runs.
 .
 Hovering a ring opens a separate detail window with the full breakdown:
 limit windows, reset times, token counts, burn rate, plan and billing
 cycle. The FreeLLMAPI variant adds router pressure, 24-hour request
 health, latency, monthly usage, per-key budgets and cooldowns. Every
 panel is positioned outside the widget and never covers it.
 .
 Claude Code data comes from claude-monitor and the local transcripts;
 Codex data from its session logs; Cursor usage is queried with the
 token already stored by the Cursor installation. FreeLLMAPI data is
 read from the local Docker container's SQLite database.
